      "label": "people dressed in Ku Klux Klan-style robes",
      "description": "Four figures standing side-by-side, wearing white hooded robes with pointed hoods covering their heads and faces, each adorned with a circular emblem on the chest. Their attire is historically associated with the Ku Klux Klan, a white supremacist organization. The figures are posed formally, suggesting a staged photograph. The visual material is black and white, indicating an early 20th-century origin, likely from a historical film or photograph. The presence of an early airplane in the background further contextualizes the image as historical. The individuals are the central focus of the image, and their attire is the most salient visual element.",
